{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "def fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number.\n    >>> fib(10)\n    55\n    >>> fib(1)\n    1\n    >>> fib(8)\n    21\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 1, 1  # a represents F(i-2), b represents F(i-1) in the sequence F(1)=1, F(2)=1\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\\\n        a, b = b, a + b  # Update to find F(i)\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/54", "solution": "def same_chars(s0: str, s1: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if two words have the same characters.\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzddeddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('dddddddabc', 'abcd')\n    True\n    >>> same_chars('eabcd', 'dddddddabc')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('abcd', 'dddddddabce')\n    False\n    >>> same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzddddabc')\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    def _get_unique_chars(s: str) -> set[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to determine the unique set of characters present in a string.\n        \"\"\"\n        return set(s)\n\n    unique_chars_s0 = _get_unique_chars(s0)\n    unique_chars_s1 = _get_unique_chars(s1)\n\n    return unique_chars_s0 == unique_chars_s1"}
